    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on Fused Silica substrate for 1550 nm LiDAR bandpass application. All 20 layer thicknesses are design variables bounded to [120, 250] nm. Use differential evolution optimizer with explicit clipping to enforce hard bounds. Evaluate coherent TMM across 1300-1800 nm wavelength range. Score candidates using three weighted objectives: (1) mean transmittance in 1545-1555 nm passband (maximize), (2) mean transmittance in 1400-1500 nm stopband (minimize), (3) mean transmittance in 1600-1700 nm stopband (minimize). Incident medium is air. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all physically valid candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
